= Charlottesville

Neo-Nazis and white supremacists have marched in Charlottesville, Virginia; a counter-protester has been killed by a car driven into the crowd. The country watches as the lines of acceptable politics are tested.

- @charlottesville_condemn: Demand universal condemnation
- @charlottesville_crackdown: Press for investigations of hate groups
- @charlottesville_street: Back mass counter-protest

@charlottesville_condemn
on-arrival: pro_democracy += 1.5; polarization += 0.5; farright_strength -= 1; suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); minority_dem += 1*(1-dissent)

We insist that leaders of both parties condemn the marchers without qualification.

@charlottesville_crackdown
on-arrival: farright_strength -= 2.5; militia_strength -= 30; federal_law_loyalty += 0.01; press_freedom -= 0.5; progressive_dissent -= 2

Federal agencies are pressed to prioritize domestic extremism.

@charlottesville_street
on-arrival: directleft_strength += 10; civic_strength += 200; polarization += 1.5; farleft_strength += 1; young_dem += 2*(1-dissent); suburban_dem -= 1*(1-dissent)

Counter-protests grow, and so does the danger of confrontation.
